users(id, email)
courses(id, title)
enrollments(user_id, course_id, enrolled_at, status)  -- primary key (user_id, course_id)

Statement: "enrolled_at belongs in enrollments rather than in users or courses, because it describes one learner in one course."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. A learner enrolls in many courses and a course has many learners, so one date column on users or on courses cannot hold one date per pair. The enrollment date is a fact about the relationship, and a many-to-many relationship with its own facts gets its own table: enrollments, with one row per learner and course. A common mistake is users.enrolled_at, which silently keeps only one date (usually the latest) for a learner with several courses.', 2, 5
