Statement: "lesson_title depends on lesson_id alone, not on the whole key (user_id, lesson_id), so this table is not in second normal form."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. With a composite key, second normal form asks every non-key column to depend on the whole key. completed_at needs both parts (when this learner finished this lesson), but lesson_title is the same for every learner of a lesson: it depends on lesson_id only. That partial dependency means the title is repeated in every progress row and will drift when a lesson is renamed, exactly like course_title in enrollments. A common misconception is that a table is normalized as long as it has a primary key; the question is what each column depends on.', 2, 5
